  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` for the coin dash game. It passes `typecheck`, but I haven't run `vite build` or loaded it in a browser, so the rendering is untested.\n\n**Rendering:** The arena, walls, player sphere and 10 gold coins are Aura3D primitives (`createAuraApp` on `#app`). `resize` is off and `pixelRatio` is 1, so the canvas keeps its 640x360 size. It uses `looks.preset(\"outdoor-day\")` for lighting, and I never checked that this preset loads without network access. `__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\n**Simulation:**\n- **Timestep:** A fixed 1/60 s step with an accumulator, clamped to 0.25 s per frame.\n- **Input:** WASD and the arrow keys move the player, with the diagonal normalised.\n- **Coins:** The 10 coins come from a seeded random generator (mulberry32), so a restart reproduces the same layout. Touching a coin gives +1 and moves that coin elsewhere.\n- **Round:** The round is 1800 frames. It ends `won` the moment the score reaches 15, otherwise `lost` at 30 s. `P` toggles pause and freezes the simulation. `R` resets score, time, status and positions.\n\n**HUD and eval hook:**\n- **HUD:** A DOM bar under the canvas shows `#score`, `#time` (time remaining) and `#status`.\n- **`window.__EVAL__`:** `state()` returns `{ score, status, time }`, with `time` as elapsed simulated seconds. `step(n)` runs `n` fixed steps immediately using whichever keys are currently held. It does nothing while paused or after the round has ended.\n\n",
